  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Can I reply to Google reviews without verifying my business?</h3>
    <p>No. Google says you must verify your business before you can reply to reviews on your Business Profile.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Why isn't my reply showing yet?</h3>
    <p>Google checks replies against its content policies before posting them. It says this usually takes up to 10 minutes but can take up to 30 days. If a reply is not approved, you are asked to edit it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Does the reviewer see my reply?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Google notifies the person who wrote the review when you reply, and they can still change their review afterwards.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h3>Can I delete a bad review?</h3>
    <p>No. You can report a review, and Google removes it only if it breaks Google's policies. Google says it does not get involved in conflicts between businesses and customers.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq" style="border:none">
    <h3>Can someone else on my team reply?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Owners and managers of a Business Profile can respond to reviews. Replies appear as the business, and the person's own name is not shown.</p>
  </div>

